3 OpenParlData

Source: OpenParlData.ch
License of the data: CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
The README files and the technical report use facts from the OpenParlData exports of 04.10.2026, 13:26 UTC. Examples are the numbers of parliaments, affairs and documents.
Exports: https://files.openparldata.ch/exports/
Changes: the project calculated numbers and shares from the exports.
`track_2a/samples/` contains files for 3 documents. For each document, it has the records of the exports (without the full text field) and the PDF text as Docling output and as atoms. It also has the eCH-0295 output of the earlier converter of 12.10.2026, which is not the product. The app makes the records of the product for the 3 samples from `track_2a/app/data/samples/`. The parliaments and executives published the documents. OpenParlData gives copies of them. The API description of OpenParlData (read on 06.10.2026) does not say if CC BY 4.0 applies to these copies. `track_2a/samples/NOTICE.md` gives the details.
`track_2a/app/data/samples/` contains the PDF of the same 3 documents (`source.pdf`) and one image of each page (`page-1.png`). The app needs them for the result view. The parliaments and executives published these PDF documents. `track_2a/app/data/samples/index.json` gives the URL of the publisher of each PDF. `track_2a/README.md` (chapter "Samples") also gives the URL of the copy of OpenParlData and the SHA-256. The licence question of the copies above applies to these files also. It also applies to the page of sample 26171 in the screenshot `docs/img/result-view.png`.
This repository contains no export file and no other PDF document. It has only the export records of the 3 samples.
The scripts in `track_2a/src/` download the exports and the PDF documents from https://files.openparldata.ch/.

4 eCH-0295

ParlPDFeCH uses the working draft eCH-0295 (version I95) of the expert group "Politische Geschäfte" of the association eCH:
https://github.com/swiss/political-affairs-ech-group, commit 3cab44d (30.09.2026). eCH-0295 is a working draft. It is not approved.
ParlPDFeCH is an independent project. It is not a product of the association eCH.
`track_2a/app/layout/quellen/` has a copy of the two files below (same SHA-256), because the app validates each record against them. The licence of the working draft is not clear. The code uses the names of fields and values of eCH-0295. For the earlier converter, `make setup` downloads the two files below and examines their SHA-256.

| File | URL | SHA-256 |
|---|---|---|
| `ech-0295_affairs/input/schema.yaml` (I95) | https://raw.githubusercontent.com/swiss/political-affairs-ech-group/3cab44d6a07f60bd8211cccdcf948717ef8fba5c/ech-0295_affairs/input/schema.yaml | 7af4c7a712f16270b653a773179d08cbd1859de053b20fe0beac6b2c2ef30d20 |
| `ech-0292_meta/input/schema_common.yaml` | https://raw.githubusercontent.com/swiss/political-affairs-ech-group/3cab44d6a07f60bd8211cccdcf948717ef8fba5c/ech-0292_meta/input/schema_common.yaml | ab6c097c41cd57c40ad175e9bb130d70f4d4d8eb85281d329bee8c53c8f08b11 |

